From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] setup: declare six as a runtime dependency

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; missing six install_requires entry]

wntr/epanet/io.py does an unconditional `import six` at module import
time, but `six` is absent from setup.py's DEPENDENCIES/install_requires
and from every EXTRAS entry. `pip install wntr[optional,test]` therefore
never pulls it in on its own, and the wheel fails at
`import wntr` with "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'six'" the
moment nothing else in the environment happens to drag six in as a
transitive dependency (e.g. via python-dateutil). Reproduces on cp312
and cp313 riscv64 in CI, where no such transitive six ends up installed;
not riscv64-specific, any environment without a stray six install hits
the same ImportError.

Add six to DEPENDENCIES so installing wntr always provides it.
---
 setup.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index 2c17443..25e4cab 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@ AUTHOR = 'WNTR Developers'
 MAINTAINER_EMAIL = 'kaklise@sandia.gov'
 LICENSE = 'Revised BSD'
 URL = 'https://github.com/USEPA/WNTR'
-DEPENDENCIES = ['numpy>=2.2.6', 'scipy', 'networkx', 'pandas>=2.0', 'matplotlib']
+DEPENDENCIES = ['numpy>=2.2.6', 'scipy', 'networkx', 'pandas>=2.0', 'matplotlib', 'six']
 EXTRAS = {
     'optional': ['plotly<6.0', 'folium', 'utm', 'openpyxl', 'geopandas', 'rasterio', 'rtree'],
     'doc': ['sphinx', 'sphinx_design', 'sphinx_rtd_theme', 'pydata_sphinx_theme', 'sphinxcontrib-bibtex'],
--
